tive solutions of the equations are involved, we see it as circle).\n\nE. \\(\\text{Graph } C\\): There is a function that is one-to-one.\n\nTo conclude the answer, since \\(\\text{Graph C}\\) is the only graph that represents a one-to-one function, \\(\\boxed{C}\\).\n\nTherefore, the graph of a function (A) \\(\\boxed{A}\\), (B) \\(\\boxed{B}\\), or (D) \\(\\boxed{D}\\) is one-to-one, thus has an inverse function.\n\\(\\boxed{C}\\)",
